		{
			"id": "114876611598170751",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114876611598170751",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-18T22:33:04.589Z",
			"content": "<p>For extra curious folks, the big ol’ PR to kick this off merged yesterday: <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/eleventy/pull/3858\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/11ty/eleventy/pull/</span><span class=\"invisible\">3858</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114876626059341081",
			"parentId": "114876611598170751",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114876626059341081",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-18T22:36:45.249Z",
			"content": "<p>Roadmap and ongoing work in the milestone here: <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/eleventy/milestone/46\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/11ty/eleventy/miles</span><span class=\"invisible\">tone/46</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114876640016716056",
			"parentId": "114876560921397181",
			"url": "https://social.lol/@ewie/114876639993758511",
			"author": {
				"name": "evie",
				"url": "https://social.lol/@ewie",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/112/273/590/711/262/861/original/24a0a6a10aa1bc49.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-18T22:40:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://neighborhood.11ty.dev/@11ty\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>11ty</span></a></span> i really don’t know how to describe as anything other than “less magic”. sorry. when i first started using eleventy i couldn’t figure out how sometimes making changes to the basic blog template would result in unsuccessful builds while other times it would work fine. i could only conclude that my mental model of eleventy was wrong and parts that i thought i could control were actually part of the “magic” and would break. this is partially a skill issue on some level. lots of people are able to use 11ty and change basic templates a bunch to suit their needs without running into the feeling i had that my site was somehow fragile and i couldn’t figure out how to implement stuff i wanted to implement without running up against the magic, but it was still something that pushed me away.</p><p>something that i really liked about switching to lume is how much more the model felt like regular js, where you could see more of the data moving around. as someone who likes a static site to feel like a series of tubes (push data in, change it, push it out), it was a lot easier to model in my head, and as a result i’ve basically never had a situation where the site didn’t build and i couldn’t figure out why.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
